        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0574" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg512"/>

                <head>No. 318.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokei, Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 13,
                        1878</date>. (Received October 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 858.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Refering further to my dispatch No. 796, in
                    relation to the assassination of his excellency Mr. Okubo, it gives me pleasure
                    to note that on the hundredth day after the death of that faithful minister it
                    pleased the imperial household of His Majesty the Emperor to present to the
                    family of the deceased 30,000 yen, as appears by a notice published in the Nichi
                    Nichi Shimbun, a paper issued in this capital. I inclose a translation of the
                    notice.</p>
                <p>According to custom in Japan, the hundredth day after the death of a friend is
                    often observed in memory of the deceased.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d323-a1.xml" xpointer="d323-a1"/>
            </div>
